  "sourceConsequences": [
    "AnatomyStage accepts HTML div attributes and merges the supplied style after its view-width custom property. FigureStage forwards that style to its outer stage div, overriding its local overflow-hidden class for this Press instance.",
    "The change removes the stage paint clip on both axes for all of its descendants, allowing the existing one-pixel focus outline and two-pixel offset to paint beyond the stage content edge. It does not change the outline itself.",
    "No control, event callback, role, accessible-name relationship, visible string, value, equation, SVG geometry or physical-method code changes. Other FigureStage instances retain the shared default.",
    "Local screen-reader-only clipping and the native method-fold clipping remain on their own elements. This style does not remove those independent clips.",
    "Overflow visible also removes the formatting-context effect of overflow hidden. The source retains the same grid/flex contents and sizes, but actual geometry, ancestor clipping and non-focus overflow still require the separately assigned browser checks. Containment assertions must remain intact."
  ],
